Great! All tests are passing now. The test suite completed successfully with 5693 tests passing. The issue was that the tests were using `MagicMock` objects without setting all the required attributes that the `assess_agent_completion` function expects. 

The problem was that when `getattr(orchestrator, "_last_loop_success_count", 0)` is called on a `MagicMock` object, it returns a new `MagicMock` instance (not `0`) because `MagicMock` creates attributes dynamically. Similarly, `getattr(orchestrator, "_last_loop_timed_out", False)` returns a `MagicMock` which is truthy (evaluates to `True` in boolean context).

The fix was to explicitly set all required attributes in the tests:
- `_last_loop_success_count` (the function checks this to determine if work was done)
- `_last_loop_timed_out` (needs to be explicitly set to `False` to avoid being truthy)

This is a good example of how `MagicMock` behavior can differ from real objects when using `getattr` with default values. The tests now properly simulate the orchestrator state by setting all required attributes.[tech_lead] completed work
